## Claim
Text: "People who do not vote for the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) in the 2020 elections will not get the COVID vaccine free of cost."
Claim author: Firoz Khan 
Claim date: October 22, 2020
Claim origin: https://twitter.com/sirfirozkhan/status/1319360671729922048

## Initial Q&A
### Did the Indian government or any state government announce a policy that would provide the COVID-19 vaccine free of cost only to individuals who voted for the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) in the 2020 elections?
Answer: No, the search result does not provide evidence that the Indian government or any state government announced a policy to provide the COVID-19 vaccine free of cost only to individuals who voted for the BJP. Instead, the BJP's election manifesto for the 2020 Bihar assembly elections promised free COVID-19 vaccines to all residents of Bihar, not conditional on voting behavior. The article quotes a BJP manifesto stating, "we will make it available to the people of Bihar free of cost," without any mention of linking vaccine access to party support. Thus, the claim is not supported by this source.

Source URL: https://www.newsclick.in/Bihar-Elections-BJP-Promises-Free-COVID-19-Vaccines-Opposition-%23-VaccinePolitics

### Which specific election in 2020 is referred to in the claim, and was that election held before or after the claim date of October 22, 2020?
Answer: The claim refers to the 2020 Bihar Legislative Assembly election, which was held after the claim date of October 22, 2020, as the polls began on October 28, 2020.

Source URL: https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/news/a-non-existent-covid-vaccine-gets-caught-in-a-political-storm/article32921495.ece

### Is there any official record, such as a government press release, legislative bill, or public statement from a BJP leader, that links free COVID-19 vaccine distribution to voting for the BJP?
Answer: No official record linking free COVID-19 vaccine distribution to voting for the BJP has been found. The search result shows that the BJP’s Bihar election manifesto promised free vaccines to all people of Bihar once approved, without any condition of voting for the party. Opposition leaders criticized this as “vaccine politics,” but no statement from a BJP leader or government press release ties vaccine access to voting for the BJP.

