### What was the official COVID-19 vaccine distribution policy in India as of October 2020, and did it include any criteria related to political affiliation or voting history?
Answer: As of October 2020, India's official COVID-19 vaccine distribution policy, as reported by government officials, stated that the central government would procure the vaccine directly and make it available free of cost to priority groups—including healthcare professionals, frontline workers, people aged above 50, and those below 50 with comorbidities—under a special immunization program. The policy explicitly did not include any criteria related to political affiliation or voting history; officials emphasized that the vaccine would be distributed fairly and equitably, and states were instructed not to create separate procurement pathways. The article notes that a controversy arose over the BJP's election manifesto promising free vaccines for everyone in Bihar, but the government's stated policy was based on priority groups, not political considerations.

Source URL: https://m.economictimes.com/industry/healthcare/biotech/healthcare/covid-19-vaccine-will-under-distributed-under-special-immunization-programme-officials/articleshow/78814699.cms

