### Did the Indian government or the BJP ever deny or refute the claim that vaccine access would be tied to voting for the party?
Answer: Yes, the BJP refuted the claim. Senior BJP leader Bhupendra Yadav clarified on Twitter that "Vaccines will be made available to all Indians at nominal costs," and BJP IT cell chief Amit Malviya added that "like all programmes, Centre will provide vaccines to states at a nominal rate," emphasizing that the free vaccine promise in the Bihar manifesto was a state-level decision, not conditional on voting for the party.

Source URL: https://www.thehindu.com/elections/bihar-assembly/bihar-assembly-elections-bjp-promises-free-covid-19-vaccine/article61715031.ece

### Are there any documented cases where individuals were denied free COVID-19 vaccines because they did not vote for the BJP in the 2020 elections?
Answer: Based on the search result, there are no documented cases of individuals being denied free COVID-19 vaccines for not voting for the BJP. The article discusses political controversy and memes around a promise of free vaccines, but it does not provide any evidence of actual denial of vaccines to non-BJP voters.

